{
  "raw": {
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Adjunct--Psychology_JREQ-002700": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Psychology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-14\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . The School of Social Sciences, Communication, and Humanities at Endicott College is currently seeking individuals to teach the following in-person courses in the Spring 2027 semester, with classes starting on January 25, 2027 and ending on May 14, 2027:  Psychology (PSY) 322 Biological Psychology Psychology (PSY) 345 Cognitive Psychology Compensation Per Course: In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the pay range for this position is $1,100–$4,700 per 3-credit course. This range reflects base pay only and is determined by course enrollment, spanning from the minimum rate for low-enrolled courses to the maximum established rate. This does not include other potential compensation or benefits.   All courses are taught in-person:  In-person lecture courses meet for 3 hours a week in either a Monday/Wednesday/Friday 50-minute format or a Tuesday/Thursday format 75-minute format. PSY 489 meets once a week on Fridays for an 85-minute block. Instructors are expected to: Deliver the course(s) in person in their assigned time blocks. Abide by Endicott’s academic policies as described in the College’s faculty handbook. Use the course description and honor the learning outcomes of each course. Use Canvas as the course’s learning management system. Meet deadlines for roster verification and submission of grades. Communicate with the dean or other administrators if issues arise concerning the teaching of specific classes. Meet with students if they request assistance or need clarification for any course-related matter, if requested. Provide samples of student work that may be used for assessment purposes. Use Endicott email when communicating with students outside of class. Qualifications: A minimum of a Master’s degree is required, and college-level teaching experience is preferred."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Adjunct--Marketing_JREQ-002699": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Marketing",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-14\nPosted: Posted Today\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . The School of Social Sciences, Communication, and Humanities at Endicott College is currently seeking individuals to teach one or more of the following in-person courses in the Spring 2027 semester, with classes starting on January 25, 2027 and ending on May 14, 2027:  Marketing Communication/Advertising (MCA) 312 Strategic Media Planning Students learn the planning process used to develop a marketing campaign. Utilizing research and data, students develop effective marketing planning. After studying case studies of real-world strategic marketing and media plans, students develop, present, and defend their own strategic marketing and media plans based on specific marketing objectives. The course emphasizes creative problem solving with hands-on group work that simulates a real-world work environment. Communication (CMM) 380 Media Ethics This course provides an overview of the ethical conflicts faced in contemporary society by media professionals. Through the application of various ethical frameworks, students consider the traditional and contemporary problems of expression and dissemination of information in a converged world. Communication (CMM) 306 Social Impact of the Media This course examines the role of media in modern culture. Students examine how media potentially impacts the development of beliefs, attitudes and behavior.  Students additionally engage in complicated examinations of media texts and their connections to appropriate political, social, and economic issues. Compensation Per Course: In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the pay range for this position is $1,100–$4,700 per 3-credit course. This range reflects base pay only and is determined by course enrollment, spanning from the minimum rate for low-enrolled courses to the maximum established rate. This does not include other potential compensation or benefits.   All courses are taught in-person:   In-person lecture courses meet for 3 hours a week in either a Monday/Wednesday/Friday 50-minute format or a Tuesday/Thursday format 75-minute format. Instructors are expected to: Deliver the course(s) in person in their assigned time blocks. Abide by Endicott’s academic policies as described in the College’s faculty handbook. Use the course description and honor the learning outcomes of each course. Use Canvas as the course’s learning management system. Meet deadlines for roster verification and submission of grades. Communicate with the dean or other administrators if issues arise concerning the teaching of specific classes. Meet with students if they request assistance or need clarification for any course-related matter, if requested. Provide samples of student work that may be used for assessment purposes. Use Endicott email when communicating with students outside of class. Qualifications: A minimum of a Master’s degree is required, and college-level teaching experience is preferred."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Associate-Dean--School-of-Business_JREQ-002684": {
      "title": "Associate Dean, School of Business",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-06\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview Reporting to the Dean of the Gerrish School of Business, the Associate Dean provides academic and operational leadership for the School’s undergraduate programs. Working collaboratively with the Dean, faculty, and administrative staff, the Associate Dean promotes academic quality, effective program delivery, and student success.   Responsibilities include academic assessment and reporting; course scheduling; recruitment, hiring, and supervision of full-time and part-time faculty; and oversight of administrative functions supporting undergraduate academic programs, advising, and student success. The Associate Dean supervises designated administrative staff and oversees several professionals who, in turn, lead La Chanterelle, Endicott’s teaching restaurant and experiential learning classroom.   The Associate Dean collaborates across disciplines and College offices to strengthen the undergraduate student experience. In partnership with the Dean, the role identifies emerging trends in business and higher education and translates them into program improvements and initiatives supporting recruitment, retention, and timely degree completion. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.   Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued.   To learn more about our employee benefits, click here .    Key Responsibilities Associate Dean, Undergraduate Programs Reporting to the Dean of the Gerrish School of Business, the Associate Dean provides academic and operational leadership for undergraduate programs, advancing academic quality, effective program delivery, and student success.   Academic Leadership and Program Operations - 25% ·         Oversee undergraduate course scheduling and program delivery. ·         Lead academic assessment, reporting, and continuous improvement. ·         Collaborate with the Dean to identify emerging trends in business and higher education and translate them into program improvements. ·         Use Workday to access and analyze academic and student data, prepare reports, and inform planning and decision-making. ·         Support budget planning and monitor expenditures within assigned areas in collaboration with the Dean.   Student Advising and Success - 20% ·         Oversee administrative functions supporting undergraduate academic programs, advising, and student success. ·         Collaborate across College offices to support recruitment, retention, and timely degree completion. ·         Address student academic concerns in partnership with faculty and appropriate College offices.   Faculty Leadership and Supervision - 25% ·         Recruit, hire, supervise, and support full-time and part-time faculty. ·         Coordinate faculty teaching assignments and promote effective instruction and professional development. ·         Foster a collaborative environment with clear expectations and accountability.   Administrative Leadership - 15% ·         Demonstrated experience supervising faculty or professional staff, setting expectations, supporting development, and addressing performance concerns. ·         Promote effective processes, communication, and collaboration across academic and administrative functions.   Community Engagement - 5% ·         Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting major events such as Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. ·  As part of the leadership team, model a strong commitment to community engagement.   Collective Bargaining Agreement and Policy - 5% ·         Develop and maintain a thorough understanding of the faculty collective bargaining agreement. ·         Apply relevant contract provisions and College policies to faculty assignments, workload, evaluation, and other supervisory responsibilities. ·         Consult with the Dean and Human Resources on contract interpretation and implementation.   La Chanterelle - A Non-Traditional Teaching Classroom/On-Campus Restaurant - 5% ·         Provide supervisory oversight of La Chanterelle’s management team, which leads daily operations, and support alignment with the School’s academic and experiential learning goals   Other Duties ·         Other duties as assigned   Reporting Structure This position reports to and works under the general supervision of the Dean of the Gerrish School of Business.   Supervisory Responsibilities Direct reports include full-time and part-time undergraduate instructional faculty and designated staff supporting academic operations, student success and advising, and hospitality operations; internship faculty report directly to the Dean.   Core Competencies ●       Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. ●       Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. ●       Communication Skills: has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. ●       Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and do things differently. ●       Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through to fruition. ●       Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. ●       Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. ●       Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills ●        Master’s degree required; doctorate preferred ●        Minimum of 8 years in higher education or a related professional setting and that experience must be relevant to academic leadership or program administration ●        Former supervisory experience required ●        Strategic planning ●        Clear written and verbal communication skills ●        Experience in conflict resolution ●        Familiarity using Workday or a comparable higher education student information system to access and analyze academic data, generate reports, and support academic planning and student success. ●        Curriculum development and assessment experience preferred ●        Student advising and retention planning ●        Interprets data accurately, identifies trends, and uses evidence to guide decisions. ●        Collective bargaining agreement interpretation skills ●        Understands protocols when handling confidential matters ●        On occasion, ability to work an evening or weekend.   In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $131,000–$165,000. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Effective Date of Current Version: October 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Advising-Coordinator---Graduate-Instruction_JREQ-002658": {
      "title": "Advising Coordinator & Graduate Instruction",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview   The Advising Coordinator & Graduate Instruction serves a dual role supporting student success through academic advising and graduate-level instruction. Reporting to the Assistant Dean of Advising and Credentialing, this position provides direct academic advising to assigned students, serves as a Core Advisor to support and guide Academic Advisors, and contributes to the development and continuous improvement of advising practices within the Institute for Applied Behavioral Science.   In addition, the position provides graduate-level instruction and thesis support within the MS program. The individual will work closely with the Assistant Dean of Research and Thesis Coordinator to support students throughout the thesis process, including providing additional academic support, assisting with thesis-related activities, and participating in thesis defenses as needed.   The position includes an instructional in-load of five thesis course sections and requires strong knowledge of applied behavior analysis, graduate education, academic advising, research, and thesis development. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.   Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued.   To learn more about our employee benefits, click here .   Key Responsibilities Academic Advising and Advising Coordination (50%) ·         Serve as an Academic Advisor and maintain regular communication with assigned advisees regarding academic progress, program requirements, performance, and overall student success. ·         Conduct an annual, in-depth synchronous advising and evaluation meeting with each assigned advisee, along with multiple points of contact throughout each semester, including synchronous meetings as appropriate. ·         Serve as a Core Advisor by providing guidance, support, information, and professional expertise to a designated group of Academic Advisors. ·         Provide consultation and support to Academic Advisors regarding student needs, academic planning, advising practices, and program requirements. ·         Attend annual academic planning meetings for students assigned to Academic Advisors within the Core Advisor structure. ·         Collaborate with the Assistant Dean of Advising and Credentialing to develop resources, tools, and support structures that strengthen the advising experience. ·         Assist with the onboarding and training of new Academic Advisors. ·         Contribute to the assessment and continuous improvement of advising practices and the overall student advising experience. ·         Identify student concerns and, when appropriate, connect students with relevant institutional resources and support services. ·         Maintain accurate and timely advising records and documentation. ·         Collaborate with faculty, staff, and academic leadership to promote student progression, engagement, and success.   Graduate Instruction and Thesis Support (50%) ·         Teach an instructional in-load of five thesis course sections within the MS program. ·         Provide graduate-level instruction, mentoring, and academic support to students enrolled in thesis courses. ·         Support students across the three thesis course experiences, including providing additional guidance to students who require assistance progressing through their thesis work. ·         Collaborate with the Assistant Dean of Research and Thesis Coordinator on thesis-related activities, student support, and program needs. ·         Assist with thesis defense preparation and participate in thesis defense coverage as needed. ·         Provide feedback and guidance to students regarding thesis development, research methodology, literature reviews, academic writing, and related research activities. ·         Support students in applying principles of applied behavior analysis and research methodology to their thesis projects. ·         Collaborate with faculty and academic leadership to promote high-quality graduate instruction and successful completion of thesis requirements. ·         Maintain appropriate instructional records and fulfill all responsibilities associated with assigned graduate courses. ·         Other duties as assigned   Community Engagement ·         Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible.   Supervisory Responsibilities ·         No supervisory responsibilities. Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through to fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge, and experience with team members.   Qualifications and Skills ·         PhD in Applied Behavior Analysis (ABA) or a closely related field, as appropriate to the program requirements. ·         Active Board-Certified Behavior Analyst–Doctoral (BCBA-D) certification. ·         Professional experience in academic advising and graduate-level instruction in higher education. ·         Demonstrated experience conducting systematic literature reviews. ·         Demonstrated experience with experimental research methodology in applied behavior analysis. ·         Strong knowledge of applied behavior analysis principles, research methodology, and graduate-level academic expectations. ·         Excellent written and oral communication skills. ·         Demonstrated ability to advise, mentor, and support graduate students effectively. ·         Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple responsibilities and deadlines. ·         Ability to work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and academic leadership. ·         Demonstrated commitment to student success, academic quality, and continuous improvement.   Preferred Qualifications ·         Experience advising graduate students in an ABA or related graduate program. ·         Experience teaching graduate-level thesis or research courses. ·         Experience mentoring students through the thesis or culminating research project process. ·         Experience participating in thesis defenses or graduate research evaluation. ·         Experience supporting or training academic advisors.   In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $65,000–$74,000. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Effective Date of Current Version:  September 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Assistant-Director--Organizational-Behavior-Science---Doctoral-Program_JREQ-002659": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Organizational Behavior Science - Doctoral Program",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Assistant Director of the Organizational Behavior Science Doctoral Program supports the academic administration, development, and ongoing operations of the doctoral program within the Institute for Applied Behavioral Science. Reporting to the Dean, the Assistant Director provides leadership and coordination in doctoral student advising and mentorship, academic programming, research development, teaching, scholarship, and professional engagement.   The Assistant Director serves as a key academic resource for doctoral students throughout their progression in the program, including comprehensive examinations, research development, Institutional Review Board (IRB) processes, dissertation preparation, publication development, and professional presentations. The position also contributes to the broader priorities of the Institute and College through teaching, scholarship, committee service, community engagement, and external relationship development.   The Assistant Director will teach four courses annually, at least three of which will be at the doctoral level; advise and mentor a minimum of nine doctoral students; support doctoral student research and professional development; participate in dissertation and academic committees; and contribute to program, department, and College initiatives as assigned. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.   Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued.   To learn more about our employee benefits, click here .   Key Responsibilities   Doctoral Student Advising, Mentorship & Academic Progress (40%) ·         Advise and mentor a minimum of nine doctoral students throughout their academic progression and professional development. ·         Serve as dissertation chair or committee member for assigned doctoral students, including reviewing dissertation proposals and drafts and participating in proposal and defense meetings. ·         Support and evaluate doctoral student readiness for comprehensive examinations in collaboration with appropriate program faculty. ·         Meet individually with assigned doctoral students on a weekly or biweekly basis, as appropriate to student needs and program milestones. ·         Facilitate weekly or biweekly research labs for assigned doctoral students. ·         Provide discipline-specific guidance regarding degree requirements, research development, professional development, and career preparation. ·         Review and support the development of IRB applications and research protocols. ·         Review and support students in developing manuscripts, publications, conference presentations, and other professional dissemination. ·         Help students identify and pursue professional development opportunities aligned with their academic, research, and career goals.   Teaching, Research & Scholarship (30%) ·         Teach four courses annually, at least three of which will be at the doctoral level. The remaining course may support departmental or programmatic needs, including master's-level instruction. ·         Develop and deliver high-quality instruction grounded in current research and evidence-based practices in organizational behavior science. ·         Maintain current knowledge of research, scholarship, and professional practices relevant to organizational behavior science, business, leadership, and related fields. ·         Engage in scholarly and professional dissemination through publications, conference presentations, invited presentations, podcasts, webinars, and other appropriate professional forums. ·         Contribute to research and scholarly initiatives within the Institute and support doctoral student engagement in research and dissemination activities. ·         Apply appropriate research methodologies, including single-subject and group experimental designs, to academic and applied research.   Program Administration & Development (15%) ·         Support the Dean in the ongoing administration, development, and continuous improvement of the Organizational Behavior Science Doctoral Program. ·         Contribute to the development and implementation of program initiatives that enhance doctoral student learning, research, professional development, and overall student experience. ·         Identify opportunities to strengthen curriculum, academic programming, student support, and professional engagement. ·         Collaborate with faculty and staff to address programmatic needs and support effective communication and coordination. ·         Participate in doctoral program orientation, graduation, and other key academic milestones. ·         Support program-related projects and initiatives as assigned by the Dean.   Departmental & Institutional Service (10%) ·         Serve on department, school, and College committees as requested. ·         Participate in departmental, school-wide, and College-sponsored conferences, academic events, and professional development activities. ·         Participate in College-wide events and activities that support the student experience and broader College community, including Commencement, Homecoming, orientation, and other institutional events as appropriate. ·         Collaborate with colleagues across the Institute and College to advance shared academic and institutional priorities. ·         Participate in faculty and staff meetings and other activities necessary to support effective program and departmental operations.   External Engagement & Partnerships (5%) ·         Support the Director of Practicum and Immersion Experiences in developing and maintaining relationships with organizations and professionals in the business and applied behavioral science communities. ·         Help identify opportunities for doctoral students to engage in immersions, applied projects, research, professional development, and other experiential learning opportunities. ·         Represent the Institute and the Organizational Behavior Science Doctoral Program professionally with external organizations, community partners, and industry professionals. ·         Contribute to the development of partnerships that strengthen the connection between doctoral education, research, and applied organizational practice.   Community Engagement ·         Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible.   Supervisory Responsibilities ·         No supervisory responsibilities.   Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through to fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members.   Qualifications and Skills ·         Doctoral degree in Organizational Behavior Management, Behavior Analysis, Organizational Behavior, Applied Behavioral Science, or a closely related field. ·         Demonstrated expertise in research methodology, including single-subject and group experimental designs. ·         Demonstrated expertise in scientific and scholarly writing and APA style. ·         Advanced expertise in conducting systematic literature reviews, including familiarity with established methodologies such as PRISMA. ·         Experience advising, mentoring, teaching, or otherwise supporting graduate or doctoral students. ·         Demonstrated scholarly or professional engagement in areas related to business, leadership, organizational behavior management, organizational behavior science, or applied behavioral science. ·         Professional experience in business, industry, consulting, research, or applied organizational settings. ·         Strong written, oral, interpersonal, and organizational communication skills. ·         Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities independently and collaboratively.   Preferred Qualifications ·         Experience teaching at the doctoral level. ·         Experience serving as a dissertation chair or committee member. ·         Experience supporting or navigating Institutional Review Board (IRB) processes. ·         Experience with data visualization and statistical software, such as GraphPad Prism, or comparable platforms. ·         Demonstrated record of publications, presentations, or other scholarly dissemination. ·         Experience working across multiple organizational or industry settings, such as healthcare, manufacturing, energy, safety, or other complex environments. ·         Experience developing partnerships with business, industry, community, or professional organizations. ·         Experience supporting doctoral program development, academic administration, or continuous program improvement.   In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $70,000–$92,000. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Effective Date of Current Version: September 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Associate-Registrar--Reporting-and-Data-Analytics_JREQ-002668": {
      "title": "Associate Registrar, Reporting and Data Analytics",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-10-01\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Job Summary Reporting to the Registrar, the Associate Registrar provides business analysis and develops data reports for the Office of the Registrar. This position also manages student enrollment and degree verification reporting to the National Student Clearinghouse, ensuring compliance with regulatory reporting requirements. Additional responsibilities include overseeing the transcript Evaluation process, and supporting the maintenance of the degree audit system and academic plans for each academic year.   Key Outcomes 50% of Time:  Develop and maintain reports that support the operations of the Office of the Registrar. ●        Gather, document, and analyze business needs and reporting requirements for the Office of the Registrar, developing new reports to support the day-to-day operations of the office. ●        Develop, maintain, and optimize reports using Workday Student reporting tools to support academic and administrative departments, as well as third-party requests and federal and state regulatory requirements. ●        Collaborate with academic and administrative offices to identify reporting needs, define requirements, and develop solutions that provide accurate and actionable information. ●        Work proactively with internal and external stakeholders to revise and deliver accurate, user-friendly institutional reports that meet operational and regulatory needs. ●        Interpret and evaluate historical data to ensure operation-critical reports are current, accurate, consistent, and available when needed. ●        Perform data validation and quality checks to identify discrepancies, investigate data issues, and ensure the accuracy and integrity of information used for reporting and decision-making. ●        Analyze existing reports and reporting processes to identify opportunities for increased efficiency, automation, and improved data quality. ●        Maintain documentation for reports, including business requirements, data sources, report logic, definitions, and standard procedures to support consistency and knowledge transfer. ●        Serve as a subject matter resource for Registrar's Office reporting and assist faculty and staff in understanding and appropriately using Registrar-related data and reports. ●        Collaborate with Information Technology and other campus partners to troubleshoot reporting issues, identify system limitations, and develop solutions to meet business requirements. ●        Monitor changes to Workday Student functionality and institutional reporting requirements and assess their potential impact on existing reports and Registrar's Office operations. ●        Provide ad hoc data analysis and reporting to support operational needs, institutional initiatives, audits, and decision-making.   30% of Time:  Generate enrollment files for submission to the National Clearinghouse (NSC). ●        Understand NSC/NSLDS regulatory and reporting requirements. ●        Responsible for submitting enrollment and graduate files on a regular schedule throughout the academic year. ●        Analyze and communicate with auditors and Registrar to quickly resolve errors that may arise during end-of-term processing. ●        Archive and track submitted reports as required by federal and state regulations.   20 % of Time:  Maintain complete and accurate documentation of technical processes used in or relevant to the Office of the Registrar. ●        Collaborate with the team to develop and maintain standard operating procedure documentation (SOPs) to ensure best practices are documented accurately on time. ●        Provide first-level customer support and troubleshoot system issues related to reporting practices. ●        Serve as liaison between the Office of the Registrar and Information Technology. ●        Support the Provost’s Office on special projects, including but not limited to preparing timely reports for Academic Review, communicating with the necessary parties in advance, holding the Academic Review sessions over the course of the academic year, sending official letters to students, and following up on particular student cases with deans. ●        Other duties as assigned.   Core Competencies   Reliability able to get the job done, available, and engaged with the job and the Endicott community Organization organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time Communication Skills   has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing Adaptability shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently Follow Through takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition Customer Service The employee anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner Initiative/Personal Leadership identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions Team Player shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge, and experience with team members   Education & Experience ●      Bachelor’s degree in Management Information Systems or related field or equivalent experience.  ●      Minimum of five years of experience in business analysis or a related field. Knowledge of higher education institutional data is preferred. ●      Minimum of three years of experience with Workday Student reporting or higher education student information systems (SIS), with experience working in a Registrar’s Office or similar academic administrative environment preferred.   Skills & Abilities ●      Sound understanding of FERPA and National Student Clearinghouse compliance. ●      Exceptional analytical and conceptual thinking skills. ●      Strong customer service skills. ●      Sound decision-making ability to determine acceptable solutions. ●      Strong written and oral communication skills. ●      Ability to work independently and in a team environment. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $72,500–$85,000. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Effective Date of Current Version: September 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Provost---Chief-Academic-Officer_JREQ-002654": {
      "title": "Provost & Chief Academic Officer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Endicott College seeks an accomplished, forward-thinking Provost and Chief Academic Officer to guide its academic strategy during a period of sustained institutional growth and innovation. Known for its required three-internship model, The Endicott Experiential Edge , the College serves approximately 3,100 traditional undergraduate students, 300 adult undergraduate students, and 1,500 graduate students across its schools and academic programs. Supported by more than $80 million in academic infrastructure investments and $20 million in campus enhancements supporting the student experience since 2019, Endicott offers a strong foundation for continued academic advancement. The next Provost will help shape the future of teaching and learning by expanding high-demand undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs; supporting faculty scholarship; strengthening interdisciplinary pathways; and preparing the College to respond thoughtfully and strategically to an increasingly AI-driven world. Endicott is a relational, close-knit global community that values accessibility, collaboration, and visible leadership. The successful candidate will be an approachable, accessible, and engaged leader who builds meaningful relationships across the College and embraces a “management by walking around” philosophy. The Provost will work closely with faculty leadership and the Endicott College Faculty Association (ECFA), fostering open communication, meaningful collaboration, and a strong commitment to shared governance. Reporting directly to the President and as a key member of the President’s Cabinet and the College’s chief academic officer, the Provost will have a significant opportunity to influence Endicott’s academic direction. The role calls for an agile and entrepreneurial leader who can bridge traditional academic affairs silos, elevate research and scholarship, and pursue strategic growth while preserving the mentor-rich, student-centered culture that defines the Endicott experience. Located just 20 miles north of Boston on a picturesque 235-acre oceanfront campus, Endicott offers its next Provost the opportunity to join a vibrant and highly collaborative community. For an inspiring academic leader who deeply respects the College’s history and traditions while eagerly embracing its future, the Endicott Provostship presents an extraordinary opportunity to make a meaningful and lasting impact. Please view the full Provost profile here . To learn more about our employee benefits, click here . Responsibilities The Provost will lead Endicott’s academic enterprise, strengthen its academic profile and operational capacity, expand institutional partnerships, and position the College for continued innovation and sustainable growth. 40%: Academic Strategy, Leadership, and Institutional Planning Develop and advance a comprehensive academic vision aligned with the College’s mission and strategic priorities. Lead academic planning across undergraduate, graduate, professional, and doctoral programs. Provide effective leadership, support, and accountability for Academic Deans and academic administrative leaders. Evaluate and evolve the academic portfolio in response to student needs, market trends, institutional priorities, and emerging opportunities. Partner with senior leadership to advance enrollment strategy, financial sustainability, and institutional growth. Ensure that academic programs maintain high standards of quality, relevance, and student success. Guide the evolution of academic programs and signature internship pathways in response to emerging technologies, while protecting academic integrity. Strengthen connections among undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. 35%: Faculty Excellence, Academic Quality, and Shared Governance Foster a culture of teaching excellence, scholarship, innovation, and continuous improvement among faculty. Serve as the College’s senior academic leader. Develop and maintain effective partnerships across the campus community, including ECFA, adjunct faculty, and academic affairs staff, advance academic priorities, and support a positive campus culture. Support effective faculty recruitment, retention, development, promotion, and recognition practices. Oversee academic policies, accreditation expectations, assessment practices, and academic integrity. Promote a collaborative environment grounded in transparency, communication, and a belief that all members of the Endicott community have an equal voice. Collaborate with administrative leaders to streamline academic workflows and operations (such as advising and administrative systems).  25%: Executive Leadership, Collaboration, and External Engagement Serve as the President’s primary advisor on academic matters and a key member of the President’s Cabinet. Collaborate equally with the President’s Cabinet across the College to align academic priorities with institutional goals. Represent Endicott’s academic mission with trustees, accrediting organizations, industry partners, donors, and external stakeholders. Champion Endicott’s distinctive experiential learning model, ensuring The Endicott Experiential Edge remains central to the academic experience. Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting major events in each division of the college. As a member of the leadership team, model a strong commitment to community engagement. Establish and maintain a robust, interactive, and transparent working relationship with the President’s Cabinet. Other duties as assigned Supervisory Responsibilities Associate Provost, Academic Affairs (overseeing academic operations, experiential learning integration, honors programs, and key academic events). Academic Deans (Undergraduate Schools, including Business, Education, Nursing & Health Sciences, Science & Technology, Social Sciences/Humanities/Communication, Sport Science, and Visual & Performing Arts).   Office Staff : Executive Assistant / Administrative Assistant  Core Competencies Strategic and Entrepreneurial Leadership :  Identifies emerging higher education trends, balances academic tradition with market agility, and translates big-picture vision into achievable operational outcomes. Collaborative Governance and Relationship Building :  Engages authentically with faculty, staff, students, and trustees; navigates complex organizational dynamics with transparency, empathy, and respect. Experiential Education Philosophy :  Possesses a deep, unwavering commitment to applied learning, profession-readiness, and student-centered outcomes. Financial and Data Literacy :  Uses quantitative and qualitative data to guide resource allocation, assess program viability, and manage complex divisional budgets effectively. Decisive and Steady Management :  Navigates ambiguity and complex institutional challenges with clear judgment, steady communication, and personal integrity. Qualifications & Skills An earned doctorate or terminal degree from an accredited institution is required. A distinguished record of teaching, scholarship or creative activity, and service appropriate for appointment as a full professor or equivalent academic standing is required. A minimum of 10 years of progressively responsible leadership experience in higher education administration. Demonstrated experience leading academic organizations, including supervising academic leaders, allocating resources strategically, and driving data-driven decisions using modern administrative systems (familiarity with or utilization of Workday preferred).  Experience developing, evaluating, and evolving academic programs in response to student needs, institutional goals, market trends, and emerging opportunities across undergraduate, graduate, professional, online, and hybrid learning environments. Demonstrated ability to foster strong relationships and work collaboratively with faculty, staff, executive leaders, staff, executive leaders, academic leaders, and campus stakeholders. Experience advancing partnerships with external organizations, including industry, community, alumni, and philanthropic partners, to support academic opportunities and institutional goals. Demonstrated ability to anticipate and navigate macro-level trends and disruptive forces in higher education, leveraging innovative approaches to adapt academic structures and program offerings for future growth.  Strong understanding of accreditation, assessment, academic quality standards, and continuous improvement practices. Exceptional written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills, with the ability to build trust, inspire confidence, and effectively engage diverse internal and external audiences. Demonstrated commitment to student success, experiential learning, and preparing graduates for professional and lifelong achievement. Demonstrated experience working collaboratively with faculty leadership, executive leadership, trustees.  Experience fostering productive relationships with faculty unions or collective bargaining units. Preferred Attributes The ideal candidate will demonstrate: A deep commitment to Endicott’s distinctive identity , including its integration of the liberal arts, professional preparation, and experiential learning. A strong academic foundation and meaningful classroom teaching experience , providing firsthand knowledge of pedagogy, student engagement, scholarship, and faculty responsibilities. An accessible and visible leadership style , with an authentic interest in participating in the life of the campus community. Emotional intelligence and thoughtful self-regulation , including the patience to listen, understand the institutional culture and history before initiating significant change. A collaborative and service-oriented leadership approach , encouraging open dialogue across faculty, staff, students, and administration while working constructively within collective bargaining structures. Intellectual curiosity , with genuine appreciation for a wide range of academic disciplines and the value of interdisciplinary collaboration. Forward-thinking adaptability in technology , recognizing the potential of emerging tools to strengthen teaching, learning, and career preparation while preserving meaningful human connection. A holistic commitment to the student experience , supporting academic achievement, student well-being, personal responsibility, and coordinated advising. Strategic ambition for institutional growth , with an interest in elevating Endicott’s regional and national profile, expanding its geographic reach, and strengthening pathways among undergraduate, graduate, and professional programs. Approachability, warmth, and authentic care for others , reinforcing Endicott’s relational culture and ensuring that people across roles and areas of the College feel seen, respected, and valued. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $285,000–$300,000 . Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Review of applications for the Provost of Endicott College will begin immediately and continue until October 24, 2026. To assure full consideration, applications should be received by October 24, 2026 at 1 p.m. EDT, and must include: • A letter of interest addressing the strategic objectives and qualifications identified in this profile; • A current curriculum vitae; and • The contact information (email and phone) for five professional references, including their relationship to the candidate. The Search Committee will not reach out until the candidate is notified."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Business-Analyst_JREQ-002652": {
      "title": "Business Analyst",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-29\nPosted: Posted 15 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview   The Business Analyst in the Information Technology department, reporting to the Director of Enterprise Applications, is responsible for the coordination, management, testing and development of ancillary applications and secondary support of the College's Enterprise Applications. The IT Business Analyst will be working with the other IT Business Analysts and Enterprise Applications developers to gather requirements, manage projects, coordinate testing, and validate data.  The IT Business Analyst will work with the College’s Functional Areas to recommend and support business process needs and improvements. This role is full-time, and will be required to be on campus a minimum of 3 days a week with the opportunity to work remotely up to 2 days a week, as agreed upon with the Reporting Manager. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.   Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued.   To learn more about our employee benefits click here .   *** To be considered for this role, a cover letter is required. In the cover letter, please articulate why you want to be considered for the role, and why working at Endicott College is interesting to you.*** Key Responsibilities   60% of Time: Workday ERP and SIS Support ●     Assist in managing Workday-related projects and enhancement request. ●     Support configuration of Workday business processes, integrations, condition rules, and validation criteria. ●     Troubleshoots and resolves complex development, testing, and production issues. ●     Create and maintain documentation for requirements gathering, business processes, integrations, procedures, and system configuration. 20% of Time: Project Management ·         Collect, analyze, and translate business requirements into user stories, workflows, business process logic, process maps, wireframes, specifications, and acceptance criteria. ·         Monitor deliverables and ensure timely completion of projects through developing project plans and monitoring performance. ·         Ensure solutions meet business needs and requirements. ·         Adhere to the College's information security policies and follow information security procedures.  ·         Consult with the College's information security staff for guidance on best practices. 10% of Time: Support Operations ·         Daily Ticket Triage: Monitor the Freshservice ticketing queue daily, conducting initial triage, troubleshooting, and independent research to resolve technical and operational issues prior to escalation where appropriate. 10% of Time: Planning and Partnership ·         Engage with internal stakeholders to determine a strategy and vision for software applications, including business needs and requirements. ·         Serve as a liaison between stakeholders and users, building strong relationships and becoming a trusted partner and subject matter expert. ·         Create and maintain business relationships with respective stakeholders on campus, and support their work and functional needs with relevant expertise.   Community Engagement ·         Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible.   Other Duties ·         Other duties as assigned   Reporting Structure Reports to the Director of Enterprise Applications. Works under general supervision   Supervisory Responsibilities None   Core Competencies   Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members.   Qualifications and Skills   ·         Bachelor's degree in related field or equivalent work experience ·         3+ years of related experience ·         Ability to use Excel and other tools to manipulate data ·         Experience with tools like Jira, Confluence, MS Project, LucidChart ·         Demonstrates strong communication and writing skills for both technical and non-technical audiences ·         Excellent problem-solving skills ·         Excellent time management and prioritization skills ·         Ability to manage multiple projects and priorities and meet negotiated timelines with high quality deliverables Preferred Experience in higher education Workday Experience   In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $75,000–$85,000. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Effective Date of Current Version:  Month, Year September 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Grounds-Equipment-Operator_JREQ-002650": {
      "title": "Grounds Equipment Operator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-22\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Grounds/Equipment Operator is responsible for maintaining Endicott College's buildings, grounds, and equipment. This role performs a variety of tasks, including landscaping, snow removal, assisting with event setup and breakdown, handling routine maintenance and minor repairs, and completing work orders. The position contributes to a functional, safe, and welcoming campus environment. Flexibility, problem-solving skills, and a collaborative approach are essential to success in this role. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits click here . Key Responsibilities Performs grounds maintenance tasks, including planting trees and shrubs, mowing lawns, trimming hedges, and collecting leaves to keep the campus looking its best. Clears snow and ice from parking lots, walkways, and other areas to keep pathways safe and accessible. Assists with setup, breakdown, and cleanup for events and functions, ensuring timely and efficient service. General laborer work includes moving and arranging furniture, equipment, and supplies as needed, in accordance with safety guidelines. Completes minor repairs and maintenance projects as assigned or in response to work orders. Troubleshoots and performs minor repairs on equipment to keep it operating properly. Picks up trash and disposes of waste daily to keep the environment clean and safe. Performs miscellaneous tasks and assignments as directed to support departmental operations. Participates in the on-call rotation policy to address urgent needs and emergencies. Performs other duties as needed to support department and campus goals. Community Engagement Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible. Other Duties Other duties as assigned Reporting Structure Reports to the Director of Grounds. Works under general supervision. Supervisory Responsibilities None Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills A minimum of two years of experience in facilities operations, grounds maintenance, or general repair work, preferably in a college or institutional environment. Proven reliability, a strong work ethic, and a consistent record of meeting job commitments and deadlines. Demonstrated ability to provide responsive, professional customer service while maintaining a positive, helpful attitude during interactions with students, staff, and visitors. Excellent attention to detail and accuracy in performing tasks and completing documentation. Strong collaboration skills, with the ability to work effectively as part of a team while remaining accountable for individual performance. Ability to work overtime or flexible hours in response to events or emergency situations. Practical skills and knowledge to perform assigned tasks effectively. Adaptability and a positive approach to handling varied responsibilities. A minimum of a High School diploma or equivalent. Ability to climb ladders, lift up to 50 lbs., and perform physically demanding tasks. Knowledge of day-to-day operations in a college environment. Must provide proof of a valid Mass. driver's license and a current DOT medical form annually. Ability to obtain and maintain a valid Department of Public Safety Hoisting License. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the hourly pay range for this position is $22.60–$25.00 per hour. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) job responsibilities, relevant experience, skills, internal equity, and external market data when determining pay. The final hourly rate is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base pay only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Effective Date of Current Version:  September 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Assistant-Coach--Men-s-Tennis--Seasonal_JREQ-002646": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Men's Tennis, Seasonal",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-16\nPosted: Posted 28 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Assistant Coach, Men’s Tennis, Seasonal, reporting to the Head Men’s Tennis Coach within the Department of Athletics, provides part-time, seasonal support for the College’s NCAA Division III men’s tennis program. The position assists the Head Coach with practices, match preparation, student-athlete instruction and development, recruiting, conditioning, and other team-related activities. The Assistant Men’s Tennis Coach works collaboratively with the Head Coach to provide a positive, competitive, and supportive experience for student-athletes while helping to maintain a program that reflects the mission and values of Endicott College and the Department of Athletics. This position is expected to work primarily during scheduled practices, competitions, recruiting activities, and other program-related activities as assigned by the Head Coach. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. Key Responsibilities Coaching and Practice Support (40%) Assist the Head Coach with the planning and implementation of scheduled team practices. Provide tennis instruction and individual or small-group coaching to student-athletes. Assist with drills, skill development, match preparation, and team activities. Provide constructive feedback and instruction to student-athletes in support of their athletic development. Help promote a positive team environment focused on sportsmanship, accountability, teamwork, and personal growth. When requested and appropriate, assist with or take responsibility for a scheduled practice in the absence of the Head Coach. Match and Competition Support (40%) Assist the Head Coach with preparation for scheduled matches and competitions. Assist with match-day organization, warm-ups, team preparation, and student-athlete support. Provide coaching and instruction during competitions as directed by the Head Coach. Assist with scouting and preparation for opponents. When requested and appropriate, assist with a match in the absence of the Head Coach. Recruiting and Student-Athlete Development (5%) Assist the Head Coach with recruiting activities and the identification of prospective student-athletes. Support recruiting communications, campus visits, and recruiting events as requested. Assist the Head Coach in providing appropriate support and mentorship to student-athletes. Serve as a positive role model for student-athletes and contribute to their overall development. Follow all applicable NCAA Division III, conference, College, and Department of Athletics policies related to recruiting and student-athlete contact. Program and Team Support (10%) Assist with team travel and transportation as assigned and as scheduling permits. Assist with equipment, supplies, uniforms, and other team needs. Help maintain organized and appropriate tennis equipment and practice areas. Assist with basic program-related administrative tasks as requested by the Head Coach. Represent Endicott College and the Department of Athletics in a professional manner at practices, competitions, recruiting events, and other assigned activities. Community Engagement (4%) Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible. Other Duties (1%) Other duties as assigned. Reporting Structure Reports to the Head Men’s Tennis Coach. Works under the general direction of the Head Coach and receives regular direction regarding coaching, recruiting, practices, competitions, and other assigned program responsibilities. Supervisory Responsibilities No supervisory responsibilities. Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills Bachelor’s degree required. Knowledge of tennis instruction, training, competition, and student-athlete development. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. Ability to effectively work with college-age student-athletes. Ability to work collaboratively with the Head Coach and members of the Department of Athletics. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Ability to work evenings and weekends consistent with the team’s practice and competition schedule. Ability to travel occasionally with the team, as assigned and as scheduling permits. Ability to comply with NCAA Division III, conference, College, and Department of Athletics rules, policies, and procedures. Uses sound judgment and discretion when handling confidential matters. Preferred Qualifications Previous collegiate tennis coaching experience. Collegiate tennis playing experience. Experience working with student-athletes in a coaching, mentoring, or instructional capacity. Experience with recruiting prospective student-athletes. Knowledge of NCAA Division III athletics. Relevant tennis coaching certifications or professional development. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the pay for this position is $2,000 per season. This pay reflects base pay only and does not include other potential compensation or benefits. Effective Date of Current Version:  September 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Assistant-Women-s-Tennis-Coach_JREQ-002644": {
      "title": "Assistant Women's Tennis Coach",
