roup coaching to student-athletes. Assist with drills, skill development, match preparation, and team activities. Provide constructive feedback and instruction to student-athletes in support of their athletic development. Help promote a positive team environment focused on sportsmanship, accountability, teamwork, and personal growth. When requested and appropriate, assist with or take responsibility for a scheduled practice in the absence of the Head Coach. Match and Competition Support (40%) Assist the Head Coach with preparation for scheduled matches and competitions. Assist with match-day organization, warm-ups, team preparation, and student-athlete support. Provide coaching and instruction during competitions as directed by the Head Coach. Assist with scouting and preparation for opponents. When requested and appropriate, assist with a match in the absence of the Head Coach. Recruiting and Student-Athlete Development (5%) Assist the Head Coach with recruiting activities and the identification of prospective student-athletes. Support recruiting communications, campus visits, and recruiting events as requested. Assist the Head Coach in providing appropriate support and mentorship to student-athletes. Serve as a positive role model for student-athletes and contribute to their overall development. Follow all applicable NCAA Division III, conference, College, and Department of Athletics policies related to recruiting and student-athlete contact. Program and Team Support (10%) Assist with team travel and transportation as assigned and as scheduling permits. Assist with equipment, supplies, uniforms, and other team needs. Help maintain organized and appropriate tennis equipment and practice areas. Assist with basic program-related administrative tasks as requested by the Head Coach. Represent Endicott College and the Department of Athletics in a professional manner at practices, competitions, recruiting events, and other assigned activities. Community Engagement (5%) Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible. Other duties as assigned. Reporting Structure Reports to the Head Women’s Tennis Coach. Works under the general direction of the Head Coach and receives regular direction regarding coaching, recruiting, practices, competitions, and other assigned program responsibilities. Supervisory Responsibilities No supervisory responsibilities Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills Bachelor’s degree required. Knowledge of tennis instruction, training, competition, and student-athlete development. Strong interpersonal and communication skills. Ability to effectively work with college-age student-athletes. Ability to work collaboratively with the Head Coach and members of the Department of Athletics. Strong organizational and time-management skills. Ability to work evenings and weekends consistent with the team’s practice and competition schedule. Ability to travel occasionally with the team, as assigned and as scheduling permits. Ability to comply with NCAA Division III, conference, College, and Department of Athletics rules, policies, and procedures. Uses sound judgment and discretion when handling confidential matters. Preferred Qualifications Previous collegiate tennis coaching experience. Collegiate tennis playing experience. Experience working with student-athletes in a coaching, mentoring, or instructional capacity. Experience with recruiting prospective student-athletes. Knowledge of NCAA Division III athletics. Relevant tennis coaching certifications or professional development. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the pay for this position is $2,000 per season. This pay reflects base pay only and does not include other potential compensation or benefits. Effective Date of Current Version:  September 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Carpentry-Supervisor_JREQ-002629": {
      "title": "Carpentry Supervisor",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted 29 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview Reporting to the Associate Vice Presidents of Facilities Operations, the Supervisor of Carpentry is a working supervisor responsible for repairs, preventive maintenance, work orders, and renovations. You will lead a skilled in-house team of carpenters and a locksmith, and coordinate with other departments to ensure that all college-owned historic and modern facilities are in good repair, remain safe, sustainable, and fully operational. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits click here . Key Responsibilities Supervise and lead the daily operations of the carpentry shop, including assigning work, scheduling staff, and ensuring quality workmanship. Maintain and repair campus facilities by overseeing and performing skilled carpentry work for academic, residential, and administrative buildings. Plan and coordinate projects, including estimating labor and materials, prioritizing work orders, and collaborating with other Facilities Management administration, trades and campus departments. Ensure a safe work environment by enforcing OSHA regulations, College safety policies, and applicable building codes. Manage shop operations, including inventory, tools, equipment, and maintenance records. Provide excellent customer service by promptly responding to maintenance requests and communicating effectively with faculty, staff, students, and contractors. Obtain quotes, coordinate with, and oversee outside contractors as necessary. Support emergency response and campus operations, including after-hours emergencies, severe weather, snow removal, and special projects. Participates in the on-call policy. Performs other duties as needed to meet the needs and goals of the department and College. Community Engagement Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and all other hands-on-deck gatherings. Show spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible. Reporting Structure Reports to the Associate Vice President of Facilities Operations Supervisory Responsibilities Supervisory responsibilities – 3 Carpenters and a Locksmith Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Resourceful: a problem solver who can make informed decisions and can juggle multiple projects. Adaptability: exhibit a willingness to implement innovative ideas while accommodating change during fluid and evolving circumstances. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills High School Diploma or equivalent. Unrestricted Construction Supervisor License (CSL). OSHA 10 or 30 Hours certifications. Typically 8-10 or more years of progressively responsible experience in commercial, institutional, or facilities carpentry. Demonstrated knowledge of building construction methods, finish carpentry, cabinetry, framing, doors, drywall, hardware, and related building systems. Ability to read and interpret blueprints, specifications, and construction documents. Experience estimating materials, labor, and project costs. Proficiency using standard carpentry tools and woodworking equipment. Strong organizational, communication, and interpersonal skills. Must be computer literate and familiar with a computerized maintenance management system (CMMS). Must provide proof of valid Mass driver's license and DOT medical form annually. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the hourly pay range for this position is $37 - $50.00 per hour. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) job responsibilities, relevant experience, skills, internal equity, and external market data when determining pay. The final hourly rate is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base pay only and does not include benefits or other compensation."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Per-Diem-Athletic-Trainers_JREQ-002298": {
      "title": "Per Diem Athletic Trainers",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-14\nPosted: Posted 30 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Per Diem Athletic Trainer in the Athletic Department, reporting to the Head Athletic Trainer, is responsible for providing temporary, on-site coverage for athletics events (in-season practices and contests, non-traditional contests, post-season contests, camps and skills clinics) for all varsity or club teams at the discretion of the Head Athletic Trainer. Duties can include care and prevention of athletic injuries, wellness promotion, examination, assessment, diagnosis, immediate care, emergency care, therapeutic intervention, healthcare organization, administration and professional responsibility for all varsity and club student-athletes and on-site practice/contest coverage. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.  Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits click here . Key Responsibilities  Provide Athletic Training Services (70%)  o Provide on-site athletic training services for practices and athletic contests hosted by Endicott College.  o Comply with all NCAA, Conference affiliated, athletic department, industry, and institutional guidelines, recommendations, and regulations.  o The employee will be a person of integrity with high ethical standards that adheres to the NATA Code of Ethics and institutional guidelines. Adheres to the state practice act, all NATA and NCAA best practices, and standing orders specified by the team physician.  o Provides counseling and education of student-athletes within the scope of practice.  Evaluate Athletic Injuries and Illnesses (20%)  o Evaluate athletic injuries and illness sustained by a varsity or club student-athlete and refer to other health care professionals as necessary.  o Provide urgent and emergent care as needed by the situation following NATA and NCAA best practices.  o Provide treatment and rehabilitation exercises for athletic injuries or illnesses as needed    Administrative Duties (10%)  o Document all injuries and treatments provided and communicate injuries with full time Athletic Training staff  o Maintain cleanliness and safety of the equipment in the Athletic Training clinic(s)  o Works with the coaching staff and other Athletic Department personnel to ensure the safety of all facilities, environments, and equipment used for intercollegiate athletics  Reporting Structure Reports to the Head Athletic Trainer Works under general supervision. Supervisory Responsibilities No supervisory responsibilities. Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community.  Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills   ● Minimum of a Bachelor’s degree in Athletic Training  ● Valid national certification from the BOC  ● Valid CPR/AED Certification  ● Valid Massachusetts State licensure through the Board of Allied Health Professionals  ● Demonstrated ability to interact effectively with college-age students  ● Strong verbal and written communication skills  ● Possesses the ability to lift heavy objects, stand for long periods, work in various environmental conditions  ● Assist injured individuals on/off playing surfaces  ● Coverage can include availability of mornings, evenings, weekends, and holidays  ● Uses sound judgment and discretion when handling confidential matters    Preferred Qualifications N/A  In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the hourly pay range for this position is $53.00 per hour. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) job responsibilities, relevant experience, skills, internal equity, and external market data when determining pay. The final hourly rate is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base pay only and does not include benefits or other compensation.   Effective Date of Current Version: December 2025"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Associate-Dean--School-of-Nursing-and-Health-Sciences_JREQ-002613": {
      "title": "Associate Dean, School of Nursing and Health Sciences",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Associate Dean of Nursing Programs is a member of the leadership team for the School of Nursing. Under the direction of the Dean and in close collaboration with the Associate Dean of Undergraduate programs is responsible for leadership and oversight of the development, implementation, and evaluation of outstanding, innovative academic programs in the School of Nursing. This position assumes responsibility for the accreditation, curriculum development, and evaluation and assessment of all program outcomes .  The Associate Dean of Nursing Programs will provide leadership and direction to faculty and professional staff in the development of initiatives and academic activities that promote student success, help to meet expected program outcomes, as well as align with the Endicott College mission to provide students with meaningful experiential learning. An academic appointment, if applicable, will be determined separately in accordance with the College’s academic appointment process.   About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.  Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits, click here . Key Responsibilities  Lead the SON in successful program-level and institutional-level accreditation activities with all accreditation and oversight boards. (40%) Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education (CCNE) Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) New England Commission of Higher Education (NECHE) Leads the SON in assessment and evaluation of all program outcomes. Develops, oversees, and implements the evaluation process of all programs, including survey development, refinement, and analysis of outcomes. Works with the Dean to develop and implement the systematic plan of evaluation and reporting to accreditation agencies. Ensure a high-quality graduate curriculum with exceptional program outcomes that features meaningful, innovative, and experiential teaching strategies in line with the mission of the School of Nursing and the college. (40%) Ensure licensure and certification success through oversight, implementation, and effective use of programs (Fitzgerald Course). Collaborate with Program Chairs regarding curricular needs for adjunct laboratory, simulation, and clinical faculty. Assist with the vetting, appointing, orienting, and mentoring of faculty members while also creating an atmosphere of inclusivity and community within the SON. Oversee regular performance evaluations of faculty and professional staff to ensure continuous improvement. Oversee direct reports and promote a positive and inclusive work environment that supports the professional growth of staff while fostering a commitment to academic innovation and excellence. Assist the Dean in development and management of the operating and capital budgets. Represent the SON in the community through participation in scholarship, service, and professional development activities that promote the school. (20%) Support Admission and Recruiting events – especially at the graduate level, which requires the Associate Dean to work very closely with the Admission/Recruiting and Marketing/Communications Department (website design) and program chairs to establish and implement effective recruiting measures for graduate programs. Attain revenue targets for the graduate programs. Advises students based on the needs of the school. Teaches 2 courses/year based on the needs of the school. Other duties as assigned Community Engagement Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting major events such as Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. As a member of the leadership team, model a strong commitment to community engagement. Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community.  Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through to fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge, and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills Doctorate in nursing or related field; experience with a professional accreditation; Effective verbal/written communication skills and proficiency in English language; Commitment to inclusive education and developing cultural competencies among faculty, staff, and students with a lens toward social justice; Documented record of academic scholarship in a related field; Demonstrated ability to mentor students at the undergraduate and graduate levels; Evidence of outstanding teaching competencies, including online, lab, and simulation; Evidence of a commitment to service; Active participation in professional organizations; Excellent interpersonal and collaborative skills with high interest in working with all levels of learners (traditional, non-traditional, and adult students); Self-directed with excellent organizational skills; Detail-oriented and student-centered are essential to the position; The position is based out of Beverly, MA; Strong computer experience, which must include the ability to work effectively with MS Office suite products, i.e., Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Google Suite (Google Drive, Docs, Sheets, Forms), and Canvas Learning Management System. Effective Date of Current Version:  September 2026 In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $125,000-$165,000. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. To apply, please submit your resume/CV and a cover letter."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Associate-Dean--Undergrad-Nursing-Programs_JREQ-002612-1": {
      "title": "Associate Dean, Undergrad Nursing Programs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Associate Dean of Undergraduate Nursing Programs serves as a member of the School of Nursing leadership team. Reporting to the Dean and working in close collaboration with the Associate Dean of Nursing Programs and the Associate Dean of the School of Nursing and Health Sciences, this position provides leadership and oversight for the development, implementation, and evaluation of innovative, high-quality undergraduate academic programs within the School of Nursing. The Associate Dean of Undergraduate Nursing Programs supports the advancement of academic excellence by guiding faculty and professional staff in the development of initiatives and academic activities that promote student success, support the achievement of expected program outcomes, and align with the Endicott College mission of providing meaningful experiential learning opportunities. An academic appointment, if applicable, will be determined separately in accordance with the College’s academic appointment process. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits, click here . Key Responsibilities Ensure a high-quality undergraduate curriculum with exceptional program outcomes, supported by meaningful, innovative, and experiential teaching strategies that align with the mission of the School of Nursing and the College. (25%) Monitor NCLEX pass rates at or above the School of Nursing’s expected level of achievement, while meeting accreditation benchmarks and state and national pass rate expectations. Support licensure success through the oversight, implementation, and effective use of student success and assessment resources, including ATI. Collaborate with undergraduate Program Chairs to identify curricular needs related to adjunct, laboratory, simulation, and clinical faculty. Assist with the vetting, appointment, orientation, and mentoring of faculty members while fostering a culture of inclusivity, collegiality, and community within the School of Nursing. Participate in hiring faculty for undergraduates and oversee their continued professional growth. Supervise direct reports and promote a positive, inclusive work environment that supports professional growth, academic innovation, and excellence. Assist the Dean with the development and management of operating and capital budgets. Ensure a positive and supportive student experience through direct oversight of student issues across all undergraduate nursing programs. (25%) Serve as the primary point of contact for undergraduate student issues in collaboration with Program Chairs, full-time faculty, academic advisors, and appropriate college departments, including Student Success, Housing, Health Services, Career Services, International Education, Community Service, the Chaplain’s Office, Athletics, the Registrar, Financial Aid, and Admissions. Provide leadership and support related to student progression, academic concerns, retention, professionalism, and overall student success across the undergraduate nursing programs. Collaborate with faculty, advisors, and college departments to address student needs in a timely, fair, consistent, and student-centered manner. Provide leadership and oversight for simulation centers and laboratories, clinical education, and internship experiences within the undergraduate nursing programs. (25%) Collaborate with the Director of Simulation and Labs and the Director of the Clinical Placement Office to ensure that: Experiential learning opportunities are meaningful, well-coordinated, and aligned with program outcomes. Clinical, simulation-based, and internship experiences strengthen students’ clinical judgment, professional development, and readiness for nursing practice. Faculty, clinical partners, and professional staff collaborate effectively to promote consistency, quality, and continuous improvement across experiential learning settings. Required accreditation processes, standards, and documentation are consistently followed, maintained, and evaluated in these areas Support School of Nursing operations, student advising, recruitment, and professional engagement through service to the school, college, and broader community. (15%) Support Admission and Recruiting events Advise students based on the needs of the school. Support the Academic Coordinator with the Course of Study and oversee student registration and scheduling concerns. Assist the SON in successful program-level and institutional-level accreditation activities with all accreditation and oversight boards. (10%) MA Board of Registration in Nursing (MABORN) Accreditation Commission for Education in Nursing (ACEN) New England Commission of Higher Education (NECHE)  Other duties as assigned. Community Engagement Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting major events such as Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. As a member of the leadership team, model a strong commitment to community engagement. Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through to fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge, and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills Doctorate in nursing or MSN with 5 years' experience in a related field; Effective verbal/written communication skills and proficiency in English language; Commitment to inclusive education and developing cultural competencies among faculty, staff, and students with a lens toward social justice; Documented record of academic scholarship in a related field; Demonstrated ability to mentor students at the undergraduate level; Evidence of outstanding teaching competencies, including online, lab, and simulation; Evidence of a commitment to service; Active participation in professional organizations; Excellent interpersonal and collaborative skills with high interest in working with all levels of learners (traditional, non-traditional, and adult students);  Self-directed with excellent organizational skills; Detail-oriented and student-centered are essential to the position; The position is based out of Beverly, MA;  Strong computer experience, which must include abilities to work effectively with MS Office suite products, i.e., Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Google Suite (Google Drive, Docs, Sheets, Forms), and Canvas Learning Management System. Effective Date of Current Version:  September 2026 In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $125,000–$165,000 Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. To apply, please submit a resume/CV and cover letter."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Assistant-Coach--Women-s-Track---Field-and-Men-s---Women-s-Cross-Country_JREQ-002461": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Women's Track & Field and Men's & Women's Cross Country",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview Under the supervision of the Head Coach, the Assistant Coach of Women’s Track & Field, Men’s and Women’s Cross-Country programs will assist in all aspects of the cross-country and track and field programs as part of the Athletics Department.  These areas include, but are not limited to, recruiting, preparing training/practice plans, team travel arrangements, and competition planning and preparation.  The successful candidate will provide strong leadership and communication skills, demonstrate a philosophy that emphasize academic priorities for student-athletes, as well as a commitment to the growth of the Endicott community.  The Assistant Coach, Women’s Track & Field/Men’s & Women’s Cross-Country will ensure an understanding and adherence to NCAA Division III principles and Endicott College’s mission statement. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits click here . Key Responsibilities Assist in organizing and administering all phases of the Cross Country/Track & Field Programs (50%) Commit to student-athlete growth and development towards academic success Assist in programming training, practice planning, and competition planning. Assist with all team operations and administrative duties. Assist with coordinating travel logistics including rentals and hotels. Retention of quality student-athletes Recruiting (40%) Communicate with prospective student-athletes via email, phone calls, and on-campus visits Attend high school competitions to meet with prospective student-athletes Maintain an organized recruiting system to ensure streamline communication between coaching staff and recruits Fulfill annual recruiting goals Community Engagement (5%) Assist Institutional Advancement in efforts to increase athletics revenue and alumni engagement (Giving Day, Golf Tournament, and other fundraising efforts). Cultivate relationships with alumni through fundraising efforts, alumni events, and outreach. Attend department meetings and be an active member of the Endicott Athletic Department. Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible. Other Duties (5%) Other duties as assigned Reporting Structure Reports to the Head Coach, Women’s Track & Field/Men’s & Women’s Cross Country, and under general supervision of the Associate Director of Athletics and Director of Athletics. Supervisory Responsibilities None Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills Bachelor’s degree required; Master’s degree preferred. 3 years coaching experience at the college level. Ability to work effectively with diverse groups and environments. Excellent verbal and written communication, interpersonal and public relations skills. Current adult CPR/AED certification. Strong organizational and problem-solving skills. Strong leadership skills. Ability to work as part of a team. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $36,000–$46,000 Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Effective Date of Current Version:  June, 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Event-Operations--Coordinator_JREQ-002611": {
      "title": "Event Operations  Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Misselwood at Endicott College is a breathtaking oceanfront estate with historic charm, offering panoramic views and serving as the premier location for world-class events in Beverly, MA. We are seeking a vibrant and dynamic individual to join our Operations Team. Reporting to the Director of Events Operations, this role will support the efforts of the Operations Team, upholding Misselwood’s reputation for superior hospitality and seamless event execution. This is an exciting entry-level opportunity for a professional with exceptional organizational, customer service, and operational skills who excels in a dynamic environment and takes pride in delivering unforgettable experiences for clients and guests. The Event Operations Coordinator supports the planning, coordination, and execution of events with responsibility for small-scale events and operations tasks. This role assists the Misselwood Events department by managing logistics, handling administrative tasks, and ensuring effective communication between professional and seasonal teams. Nestled on the scenic coast, Misselwood Events is more than just a venue – it’s a destination where memories are made. As part of the Endicott College community, we offer a collaborative and professional environment that celebrates creativity and teamwork while delivering exceptional service.   Key Outcomes                                                                                                                     60% Logistics Coordination Coordinate and implement all details for Endicott-hosted programs, Misselwood events series, and small scale corporate day and overnight programs Perform administrative support tasks, including managing inbox correspondence, processing invoices, and maintaining operational records. Assist with scheduling seasonal staff Serve as a liaison between professional staff and seasonal team members to ensure clear communication and efficient event execution. Support Event Operation Managers will logistics and operational tasks 40% On-Site Operations Support the Operations Management team in ensuring the Misselwood House is ready to welcome guests and that day-to-day operations run smoothly. Assist with venue setup and teardown, ensuring all materials, signage, equipment, and supplies are in place before, during, and after events. Maintain inventory, submit maintenance requests, and support operational needs Perform other duties as assigned to contribute to the successful execution of events and daily operations. Core Competencies Reliability able to get the job done, available, and engaged with the job and the Endicott community Organization organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time Communication Skills has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing Adaptability shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently Follow Through takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition Customer Service customer-focused with a passion for delivering exceptional service. Employee anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner Initiative/Personal Leadership identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions Team Player shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members   Knowledge/Skills/Abilities                                                                                                                     Bachelor’s degree in event management, hospitality, or a related field is required. 1-2 years of experience in event coordination, customer service, or related field is preferred. Availability to work evenings, weekends, and flexible hours as needed. Physical ability to lift up to 40 pounds and remain on your feet for extended periods. Proven ability to manage multiple events simultaneously in a fast-paced, deadline-driven environment. Exceptional customer service skills with a proactive, solution-oriented approach. Strong written and verbal communication skills, with keen attention to detail and accuracy. Outstanding organizational and time management skills, with the ability to prioritize tasks and remain composed under pressure. Proficiency in Google Workspace and adaptability to new platforms. Ability to take initiative, think proactively, and maintain professionalism during stressful situations. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills. Commitment to timely and respectful communication, including responding to emails and voicemails. ServeSafe, Crowd Manager, and AED/CPR certifications (or willingness to obtain). In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $50,000–$60,000. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Cummings-Center-for-Nursing-and-Health-Sciences/Assistant-Professor--Doctor-of-Nursing-Practice--DNP-_JREQ-002184-1": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . The Assistant or Associate Professor of Nursing teaches courses for the Graduate Nursing Program. They also advise students, participate in accreditation processes; engage in professional scholarship or development, assist in the development of internship relationships and student opportunities, and participate in school and college-wide service. They will teach courses and advise students for two semesters.   This position is covered by the Collective Bargaining Agreement between the Endicott College Faculty Association (ECFA) and Endicott College. ECFA is a faculty union organized under the NEA (National Education Association) and provides structure and support for all full-time faculty at Endicott College.  The Cummings School of Nursing and Health Sciences is seeking a dynamic, full-time DNP Faculty member passionate about shaping the next generation of healthcare executives and clinical experts. As a vital educator in our growing Doctor of Nursing Practice program, you will leverage your expertise in healthcare leadership and clinical inquiry to teach advanced courses in both quantitative and qualitative methodologies. If you are ready to inspire doctoral students and drive innovation in healthcare delivery, this is your opportunity to make a lasting institutional impact. In this pivotal role, you will directly influence patient outcomes by championing Evidence-Based Practice (EBP) and Quality Improvement (QI) initiatives within our curriculum. You will have the opportunity to mentor, advise, and guide students through their culminating DNP Scholarly Practice Projects, translating evidence based practice into real-world clinical solutions. If you hold a Doctor of Nursing Practice degree, possess a strong background in organizational leadership, and thrive in a collaborative academic environment, apply today to join our forward-thinking nursing faculty. This is a year round position. Responsibilities include:  Teach 24 credits per academic year -- 12 credits in both the fall and spring semesters (4 lecture courses each semester, or equivalent). Advise up to 25 students.  Attend department, school, and college meetings.  Participate in accreditation processes.  Engage in professional development, scholarship, research, and/or publishing.  Assist in curriculum development.   Participate in department, school, and college service.  Maintain and post regular office hours.   Perform other duties as required and as outlined in the Collective Bargaining Agreement between the Endicott College Faculty Association (ECFA) and Endicott College.  Participate in course development and implementation.  Evaluate teaching/learning activities  Participate in governance, including the School of Nursing All School Committee and other committees as appointed   Requirement / Qualifications A doctorate in Nursing or a related field is required Must have or be eligible for RN licensure in Massachusetts Hold at least one graduate degree in nursing in the area of specialization required for the faculty appointment 3-5 years of experience in the related field of nursing Prior teaching experience in a nursing program is desired, and required at the Associate Professor Level Demonstrated ability to relate to a diverse student body Commitment to scholarship appropriate to the rank Demonstrate excellent interpersonal and collaborative skills In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the compensation for this faculty position is established through the College’s contractual salary structure. Pay rates are set for each faculty rank and appointment type. This position carries a fixed annual salary of $98,602.12 (Assistant Professor) or $115,161.61 (Associate Professor) for a 12-month appointment. This amount represents base salary only and does not include benefits or other forms of compensation."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Director--Criminal-Justice-Graduate-Program_JREQ-002538": {
      "title": "Director, Criminal Justice Graduate Program",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-29\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Director of the Criminal Justice (CJ) Graduate Program in the School of Social Sciences, Communication, & Humanities reports to the Associate Dean. The Director is responsible for leading the strategic launch, growth, and daily operations of a newly designed CJ Graduate Program, which features a soft launch in Spring 2027 and full implementation in Fall 2027. This role includes managing curriculum development, supervising full and part-time faculty, overseeing program evaluation/accreditation, and driving student enrollment and retention. This is an in-person, on-campus position. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits, click here . Key Responsibilities Dedicated to Student Success (30%) Directs graduate academic advising, guiding students from admission through progression and successful completion of their degree. Implements a proactive advising model, including onboarding new advisees prior to program entry and conducting regular progress checks. Collaborates with the Associate Dean to identify, support, and coach at-risk students to maximize retention. Maintains high-quality advising standards to ensure timely student progress through coursework and career alignment. Contributes to the overall success of the CJ graduate program (30%) Leads the successful implementation and execution of the new CJ graduate program’s soft launch (Spring 2027) and full launch (Fall 2027) in coordination with the Associate Dean. Partners closely with the Homeland Security Graduate Program Director to integrate existing HLS concentration courses into the CJ curriculum and provide seamless cross-program pathways for students. Collaborates with the Director of the Cybercrime Forensics Lab to coordinate the cybersecurity concentration, including lab exercises, simulations, and hands-on training. Drives recruitment, enrollment growth, and student retention initiatives to sustain an 80%+ retention and graduation rate. Manages ongoing program assessment, continuous improvement, and accreditation efforts at the course, program, and school levels. Contributes to the College community through service on school-wide and institutional committees. Teaches and develops courses in CJ/HLS graduate programs (20%) Teaches 2 graduate-level courses per year across the CJ and HLS programs. Demonstrates excellence in teaching through strong student evaluations and the utilization of diverse, effective assessment strategies. Develops cutting-edge course content and materials aligned with current industry trends, program needs, and School standards. Supervises, trains, and evaluates adjunct faculty (10%) Collaborates with the Associate Dean to recruit, hire, train, and evaluate part-time adjunct faculty within the CJ graduate program. Ensures all adjunct faculty align their courses with Canvas LMS standards and School pedagogical benchmarks. Reviews student course evaluations annually with faculty to implement data-driven pedagogical adjustments. Increases Endicott’s reputation in the field of CJ graduate education (10%) Maintains an active track record of scholarship and research in criminal justice or a related field. Represents the College and its graduate programs through the presentation of academic scholarship at national and state conferences, seminars, or through peer-reviewed publications. Other duties as assigned. Community Engagement Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting major events such as Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. As a member of the leadership team, model a strong commitment to community engagement. Reporting Structure The Director of the Criminal Justice Graduate Program in the School of Social Sciences, Communication, & Humanities reports to the Associate Dean. Supervisory Responsibilities Collaborates with the Associate Dean to hire, supervise, train, and evaluate 100% of part-time graduate adjunct professors. Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective, and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge, and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills Ph.D. or terminal degree in Criminal Justice, Criminology, or a closely related field highly preferred ; a Master’s degree or JD with significant academic leadership and operational experience considered. Documented record of academic scholarship and active participation in national or regional professional organizations. Demonstrated excellence in graduate-level teaching, including experience with online, lab-based, or hybrid simulation models. Strong collaborative skills with a proven ability to work across departments (e.g., working alongside Homeland Security or Cybersecurity disciplines). Commitment to inclusive education, social justice, and developing cultural competencies among a diverse, non-traditional, and adult student population. Excellent organizational and technical proficiency, including experience with Canvas LMS, MS Office, and Google Workspace. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the annual base salary range for this position is $94,000 .00   and $115,000.00. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) the scope and responsibilities of the position, relevant work experience, education, specialized skills, internal equity, and external market data when extending an offer. The final salary is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base salary only and does not include benefits or other compensation. Effective Date of Current Version:  July 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Assistant-Coach--Roller-Hockey--Seasonal-_JREQ-002134-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Coach, Roller Hockey (Seasonal)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-22\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview The Assistant Roller Hockey Coach in the Athletic Department, reporting to the Associate Director of Athletics collaborates with the athletics department advisor and team leaders to set goals, develop budgets, evaluate organizational needs, problem-solve, and serve as a liaison with other college departments essential to program implementation and success.This is a part-time, seasonal position and is a fantastic opportunity to work with a thriving collegiate club to play a key role in the clubs continued development and success. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees. Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued. To learn more about our employee benefits click here . Key Responsibilities The Assistant Coach will be inheriting a group of highly talented and motivated men that have continued to compete at Nationals every year. Coaching Duties (80%) Providing instruction, mentoring and guidance to student athletes to allow them to develop their athletic skills and abilities to maximum potential. Evaluating athletic ability and performance. Assuring that equipment and practice plans are prepared in advance of practice sessions. Maintaining positive and professional relations with students, athletes, and alumni Ability to teach safe and proper technique to beginning level players while challenging and integrating the skills of higher-level players Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible. Other duties as assigned Program Administrative Support (20%) Coordinate scheduling, meals, transportation, etc for all team trips in conjunction with the head coach Track team expenses and process invoices Please note: Under the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), position descriptions should focus on essential functions , those that, if removed, would fundamentally change the job. Reporting Structure Reports to the Associate Director, Athletics. Works under general supervision. Supervisory Responsibilities None Core Competencies Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members. Qualifications and Skills Minimum education or training needed to be considered for the role At least one year of relevant experience Specific skills or qualifications necessary to be successful If applicable, note any travel, evening, or weekend requirements If the role involves working with sensitive information, include: “Uses sound judgment and discretion when handling confidential matters” In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the pay range for this position is $2,000–$2,500 per season. This range reflects base pay only and does not include other potential compensation or benefits."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Adjunct--Architectural---Design-Studies_JREQ-002418": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Architectural + Design Studies",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-20\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . The School of Visual + Performing Arts, Department of Architectural + Design Studies is currently seeking individuals to teach undergraduate and graduate Architectural Studies and Interior Architecture courses for the 2026-2027 academic calendar year. We are seeking multiple adjunct instructors for foundational architectural studies courses and major-specific courses for the following Undergraduate Architectural Studies and Interior Architecture Majors : Architectural Sketching (4-hour studio) Building Information Modeling (REVIT and RHINO) (4-hour studio) Interior Hospitality Studio (6-hour studio) Graduate Interior Architecture: Graduate Design Theory All courses are in-person unless noted otherwise. Each lecture course meets as indicated above. In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the pay range for this position is $4,700-$4,800 per course. This range reflects base pay only and does not include other potential compensation or benefits. Instructors are expected to: Deliver the course(s) in person in their assigned time blocks through the entire semester. Abide by Endicott’s academic policies as described in the College’s  Faculty Handbook . Use the course description and honor the learning outcomes of each course. Use Canvas as the course’s learning management system. Meet deadlines for roster verification and submission of grades. Communicate with the dean or other administrators if issues arise concerning the teaching of specific classes. Meet with students if they request assistance or need clarification for any course-related matter, if requested. Provide samples of student work that may be used for assessment purposes. Use Endicott email when communicating with students outside of class. Qualifications: A minimum of a Master’s degree is required, and college-level teaching experience is preferred."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Bartender_JREQ-002335-1": {
      "title": "Bartender",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-07\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview Misselwood at Endicott College is a breathtaking oceanfront estate with historic charm, offering panoramic views and serving as the premier location for world-class events in Beverly, MA. We are seeking bartenders to work our weddings and events during the season.  This role requires work on weekends. About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.   Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued.   To learn more about our employee benefits click here .   Key Responsibilities     ·        Responsibly serve alcoholic and non-alcoholic beverages to event guest ·        Accurately check IDs ·        Responsible for monetary transactions while operating the cash register ·        Perform the set up and break down of the bar ·        Cleaning and ensuring dish machine is turned off at the end of the night ·        Responsible for counting empty beer bottles and soda bottles for event inventory sheet ·        Responsible for refilling the juice, sodas, beer and wine behind the bar for events ·        Restocking and keeping track of inventory needs ·        Other duties as assigned   Reporting Structure Reports to the Director of Event Operations. During events, will take direction from head bartender     Supervisory Responsibilities No supervisory responsibilities   Core Competencies     Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members.   Qualifications and Skills   ·        18 years or older ·        ServeSafe or TIPS certified required ·        Must be able to work late hours ·        Must be able to work weekends and holidays ·        Required to stand for long periods of time ·        Must be able to lift up to 35 pounds ·        Excellent communication and customer service skills In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the hourly pay for this position is $6.75 per hour PLUS tips. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) job responsibilities, relevant experience, skills, internal equity, and external market data when determining pay. The final hourly rate is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base pay only and does not include benefits or other compensation.   Effective Date of Current Version:  March 2026"
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Adjunct--Graduate-School-of-Education_JREQ-002332": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Graduate School of Education",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-12\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . The School of Education is currently seeking individuals to teach the following content in the Fall semester, with classes starting on September 1, 2026 and ending on November 23, 2026: School Counseling  LMHC courses  COMPENSATION PER COURSE:  In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the pay range for this position is $1,100–$4,700 per 3-credit course . This range reflects base pay only and is determined by course enrollment, spanning from the minimum rate for low-enrolled courses to the maximum established rate. This does not include other potential compensation or benefits.   All courses meet online.  Instructors are expected to: Deliver the course(s) in person or online in their assigned time blocks. Abide by Endicott’s academic policies as described in the College’s faculty handbook. Use the course description and honor the learning outcomes of each course. Use Canvas as the course’s learning management system. Meet deadlines for roster verification and submission of grades. Communicate with the dean or other administrators if issues arise concerning the teaching of specific classes. Meet with students if they request assistance or need clarification for any course-related matter, if requested. Provide samples of student work that may be used for assessment purposes. Use the Endicott email when communicating with students outside of class. Qualifications: A minimum of a Master’s degree is required, and college-level teaching experience is preferred. This program requires a MA license in School Counseling or LMHC."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Adjunct--Undergraduate-School-of-Education_JREQ-002333": {
      "title": "Adjunct, Undergraduate School of Education",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-12\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . The School of Education is currently seeking individuals to teach the following course beginning in the Fall semester, with classes starting on September 1, 2026 and ending on December 18, 2026: ED222- Culturally Responsive Pedagogy (Time TBD) ED215- Creative Arts in the Early Childhood or Elementary Classrooms (MW 2:00-3:15) COMPENSATION PER COURSE:  In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the pay range for this position is $1,100–$4,700 per 3-credit course . This range reflects base pay only and is determined by course enrollment, spanning from the minimum rate for low-enrolled courses to the maximum established rate. This does not include other potential compensation or benefits.   All courses meet in-person:  In-person lecture courses meet for 3 hours a week in either a Monday, Wednesday, Friday 50-min block or a Tuesday/Thursday format 75-min block. Instructors are expected to: Deliver the course(s) in person or online in their assigned time blocks. Abide by Endicott’s academic policies as described in the College’s faculty handbook. Use the course description and honor the learning outcomes of each course. Use Canvas as the course’s learning management system. Meet deadlines for roster verification and submission of grades. Communicate with the dean or other administrators if issues arise concerning the teaching of specific classes. Meet with students if they request assistance or need clarification for any course-related matter, if requested. Provide samples of student work that may be used for assessment purposes. Use the Endicott email when communicating with students outside of class. Qualifications: A minimum of a Master’s degree is required, and college-level teaching experience is preferred."
    },
    "https://endicott.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/Endicott/job/Endicott-College-Main-Campus/Banquet-Server--Part-time-_JREQ-002308-2": {
      "title": "Banquet Server (Part-time)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-02-25\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nWe are located approximately 20 miles north of Boston and parking is free. We are also accessible by commuter rail on the Newburyport/Rockport line. Come and explore Endicott’s seaside locale where employees are an important part of the bustling campus community! Please apply today if this opportunity looks like the right fit for you. . Position Overview   The Wylie Inn and Conference Center is seeking Full Time Banquet Servers to join their team of dedicated professionals The Wylie Inn & Conference Center employees are part of the Endicott College community and share in the beautiful campus offerings. Endicott is located 20 miles north of Boston and accessible by public transportation. The parking is free and the beautiful beaches are close by! Situated on a picturesque stretch of the Atlantic Coast on Boston’s North Shore, the Wylie Inn and Conference Center at Endicott College offers well appointed, comfortable accommodations with an on-site café restaurant and bar; state of the art IACC certified conference center and an elegant social event venue, upper Manor. The Wylie Inn and Conference Center is ideal for a weekend getaway, retreat or conference. This lush 10-acre inn and conference center is just minutes away from historic downtown Salem, restaurants, scenic Cape Ann, shopping, museums and more.   About Endicott College Endicott College is a vibrant community located on Boston’s North Shore, with a beautiful oceanfront campus in Beverly, Massachusetts. We’re known for combining academic excellence with hands-on learning, and we take pride in fostering a supportive environment for both students and employees.   Working at Endicott means joining a close-knit campus community where your contributions matter and where collaboration, creativity, and professional growth are valued.   To learn more about our employee benefits click here .   Key Responsibilities   ·        Set up banquet room as instructed by Banquet Captain to include linen, service ware and glassware ·        Attend roll call meetings before events to learn function particulars, including guest and hotel expectations ·        Greet guests and respond to requests in a friendly and courteous manner ·        Serve the food and/or beverage in the order and to the expectation of the Banquet Captain to ensure consistency in the order throughout the banquet ·        Promptly bus dishes as guests complete each course and/or meal at the end of the meal or function   Community Engagement Be an active participant in the life of the College by attending and supporting key events like Commencement, Homecoming, and other all-hands-on-deck gatherings. Show a spirit of collaboration and community involvement, including volunteering when possible.   Other Duties   ·        Other duties as assigned   Reporting Structure Reports to the Food Director with Direct Supervision   Supervisory Responsibilities   No supervisory responsibilities.   Core Competencies   Reliability: able to get the job done, available and engaged with the job and the Endicott community. Organization: organizes time and resources well so that work is done efficiently and on time. Communication Skills: has clear, effective and efficient ways of communicating, both orally and in writing. Adaptability: shows a willingness to adopt new ideas and to do things differently. Follow Through: takes ownership of projects and sees them through fruition. Customer Service: anticipates the needs and responds to queries in a timely, competent, and approachable manner. Initiative/Personal Leadership: identifies opportunities for improvement and actively contributes to solutions. Team Player: shows a willingness to collaborate and share information, knowledge and experience with team members.   Qualifications and Skills   ·        Minimum 18 years old ·        Ability to work in a standing position for long period of time ·        Ability to lift up to 25 pounds, maneuvering trays of food and drink ·        Ability to work well under pressure in a high-volume event ·        Positive attitude In compliance with Massachusetts pay transparency law, the hourly pay for this position is $18.50 per hour, increasing to $21.50 for Wedding events. Endicott College considers factors such as (but not limited to) job responsibilities, relevant experience, skills, internal equity, and external market data when determining pay. The final hourly rate is determined by the Human Resources Office based on these factors. This range reflects base pay only and does not include benefits or other compensation.   Effective Date of Current Version:  February 2026 To be considered for this role, please submit an application and include a resume. Please Note: All employees must be 18 years of age or older."
    },
